%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0ca23d3e41cd5424c9ec72c610ef25a4, type: 3}
  m_Name: NatsukiTakesNotes
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  autoFocusSpeaker: 1
  screens:
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614614
    - rid: 1790118786062614615
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: (I guess this is my room now, huh...)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614616
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: Take a seat, we might as well be comfortable during your instruction.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614617
    - rid: 1790118786062614618
    - rid: 1790118786062614619
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: The first thing you need to understand about being a Harbinger is your
      role.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614620
    - rid: 1790118786062614621
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: 'As you, hopefully, know, the Harbinger is not a leader in the traditional
      sense:'
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: The Harbinger does not dictate instructions and commands onto their fellow
      Companions.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: The Harbinger <i>can</i> be considered a leader in terms of determining
      what it means to be a Companion.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614622
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: How so?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614623
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: 'An example, then:'
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614624
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: Mryfwiil the Withdrawn was one of the earliest Harbingers, living only
      a few hundred years after Ysgramor's death.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: During his time, the Companions were all but a collection of swords-for-hire,
      who would take on any job for the coin and honor.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: This meant that they were often sought after to fight in wars, often
      with Companions being paid to fight on different sides of the same war.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: You can see where the problems begin- how are we supposed to act as Shield-Siblings
      while warring against each other for personal gain?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: To prevent this, Mryfwiil declared that the Companions would never take
      on any war or political conflict.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: Of course, that doesn't stop certain members of the Companions participating
      in war as they deem worthy-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: I would know, that's how my father passed to Sovngarde-
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614627
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: But, as a group of Shield-Siblings, we do not find honor in fighting
      for such purposes.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614628
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: Myrfwiil shaped the definition of a Companion to no longer include mercenary-of-war,
      so have all Harbingers in the ways they see fit.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: But what if there's nothing major I need to decide on like that?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614629
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: In that case, you'd join the ranks of most of our Harbingers.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614630
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: Those sorts of sweeping decrees only occur in times of crisis; a measure
      only as drastic as its moment.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: It's far more likely you'll have to act in petty matters; if a particular
      job comes in whose honor seems dubious, you decide if it should be taken or
      not.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: So I'm sort of like a judge?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614631
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: I suppose so.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614632
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: How do the Companions even get jobs anyway?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614633
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: It's good that you mention that, that will be part of your responsibility.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614634
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: People from all across Skyrim, and even sometimes beyond, are able to
      commission us for our services.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: They do so by either sending us a writ of work, or by coming in person.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: It is customary to include the specific price they will pay as part of
      the request.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: The Harbinger decides if the Companions should take on the job or not,
      depending on the honor of the task.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: If it's honorable, the task gets given to one of the Circle members to
      be distributed-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: Otherwise, the Harbinger will send a message of decline.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: You don't <i>need</i> to give a reason why, but it is good to do so for
      posterity.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: The Harbinger also has the responsiblity of renegotiating terms if they
      seem unreasonable- especially concerning payment.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: If the job is taken on and successfully completed, a portion of the job's
      profit is immediately given to the Companion who did the job.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: Wait, but you haven't mentioned the person who requested the job paying
      anything yet?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614635
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: That's correct, we pay our own before the group itself receives payment
      for completion of the job.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614637
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: When the job is done, the Harbinger sends back word to the person who
      requested the job-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: Who will then send the septims, if they know what's good for them.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: I take it if they don't pay, some capable warriors will find their way
      to their doorstep?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614638
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: Indeed. Which is why very few are foolish enough to withold our payment;
      they know who they're dealing with.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614639
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: Isn't it a bit dangerous to pay our people before we get the money?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614640
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: It would be, if our coffers aren't effectively maintained.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614641
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: Which is, again, part of your responsibility.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614642
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: The Harbinger keeps track of and manages our expenditure.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614643
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: Which is only as hard as you make it- you don't <i>need</i> to change
      our spending from where Kodlak left it.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: What <i>are</i> we currently paying for?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614644
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: 'We''ve only got a few people directly on a payroll:'
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614645
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: Tilma the Haggard, who I'm sure you know keeps this place clean and in-order-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: And Eorlund, who we pay monthly to take care of our arms, which is a
      discount compared to everyone paying for their own gear.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: The other main source of costs comes from getting Tilma cleaning supplies,
      keeping our banquet full, and making sure the fire's warm.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: We already have pre-existing arrangements to get most of those, so the
      cost isn't much compared to what we make.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: All left-over funds are technically yours to spend, but I'd advise against
      giving into unearned avarice-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: It wouldn't look good before your fellow Companions.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: 'So let me get this straight:'
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614646
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: 'My duties as Harbinger include: being a judge, a contract negotiater,
      and an accountant?'
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614647
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: A bit mundane when you put it like that, I admit, but what comes along
      with it is the highest honor of the mightiest warriors of Tamriel.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614648
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: Yeah...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: (How long has it been since I've done math without a calculator...?)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: This has been enough talk for now.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614649
    - rid: 1790118786062614650
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: Come on, let's go get some practical experience-
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614651
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: We've received a job offer, and you should decide what we do with it.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614653
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 639d4037fbc3acd41947392e6542aac6, type: 2}
    dialog: Natsuki reads the request...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614654
    - rid: 1790118786062614656
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: So?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614655
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: The Rift is the province that Riften is the capital of, right?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614657
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: That's right, is that where the request is leading us?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614658
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: Basically, they're offering us two thousand septims to go into a Nordic
      ruin called Forelhost to go murder a dragon priest.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614660
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: A dragon priest? Mighty prey indeed, especially since we'll have to fight
      our way through draugr to reach them.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614661
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: As part of the request, we have to deliver the dragon priest's mask to
      their homestead, Snow-Shod Farm, as proof the deed is done.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614662
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: ... they want the mask, specifically?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614663
    - rid: 1790118786062614664
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: Is there something notable about that?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614665
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: Indeed, the masks of dragon priests are rumored to hold incredible power.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614666
    - rid: 1790118786062614667
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: So to request <i>that</i> specifically as proof, when we could bring
      along the dragon priest's clothes and ashes, is... concerning.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: They said that they wanted us to kill the dragon priest to make sure
      that the draugr don't bother them anymore.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614668
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: Hm. The draugr have never once been reported to leave their tombs; they
      are consistent in their vigil, after all.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614669
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: This request has more than meets the eye, that's for sure-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: So, what shall we do?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614670
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614671
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: I think we should take on the job.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614672
    - rid: 1790118786062614673
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: Why?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614674
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: First, on the highly-unlikely chance that draugr are actually wandering
      about, we should take care of that; not everyone can...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614675
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: Second, two thousand septims is a hefty payout, I doubt these sorts of
      contracts come around often...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: Third, we can learn more about this potential power-hungry maniac living
      in the Rift, and make sure they aren't doing anything dangerous.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: We don't <i>need</i> to give them the mask to prove we killed the dragon
      priest, do we?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614676
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: That way we can tell if they're after the mask for nefarious purposes,
      or <i>just</i> proof.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: Any complaints?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614677
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: None. I doubt anyone else would, either.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: So are you going to go tell Farkas and Aela to get this job out to the
      others, or-?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614678
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: I don't think we should, this job is probably too intense for most of
      our warriors to do alone.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614679
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db46f9c9f9769b944946c389f5c0fbec, type: 2}
    dialog: We should gather the Circle to take care of this.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: Ah, fair enough.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614680
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614682
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 639d4037fbc3acd41947392e6542aac6, type: 2}
    dialog: 'As Natsuki and Vilkas enter the dining hall, they find a bit more rabble
      than usual: three simultaneous and separate brawls.'
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614683
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: Aela! Farkas! Get over here!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614684
    - rid: 1790118786062614685
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 17bd3b6fcae930647918fc183fea836b, type: 2}
    dialog: Aye?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614686
    - rid: 1790118786062614687
    - rid: 1790118786062614688
    - rid: 1790118786062614689
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 6f47b2f061a0a3249992cdd21d6995ed, type: 2}
    dialog: Need something?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614691
    - rid: 1790118786062614692
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: Yeah, we've got a big job ahead of us...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614693
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 639d4037fbc3acd41947392e6542aac6, type: 2}
    dialog: Natsuki recounts the details of Valmir's request, Vilkas' concerns, and
      the plan to follow through.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614694
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 6f47b2f061a0a3249992cdd21d6995ed, type: 2}
    dialog: Already dealing with this much intrigue on your first day as Harbinger?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614695
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 6f47b2f061a0a3249992cdd21d6995ed, type: 2}
    dialog: I'm not sure if you're lucky or not...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614696
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 17bd3b6fcae930647918fc183fea836b, type: 2}
    dialog: What are we waiting for? We should get moving.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9f0072f96d4dfc24f9477258c07882f5, type: 2}
    dialog: Not until I've had lunch, you dingus.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614697
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 17bd3b6fcae930647918fc183fea836b, type: 2}
    dialog: Oh. Okay.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118786062614698
